      "title": "Embattled Greens senator Jordon Steele-John confirms leave from parliament after allegations against him made public",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/24/greens-senator-jordon-steele-john-confirms-leave-from-parliament-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>WA politician says he considered attending Senate estimates virtually but was told it would be ‘unacceptable’</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Jordon Steele-John has confirmed he will not attend parliament next week as the embattled Greens senator apologises for publicly releasing the letter outlining the claims against him.</p><p>On Saturday afternoon, Steele-John removed a social media post containing a three-page letter marked as “confidential” sent to the Greens leader, David Shoebridge, earlier this month. The letter urged an investigation into allegations he had acted inappropriately towards women between 2017 and 2025.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/24/greens-senator-jordon-steele-john-confirms-leave-from-parliament-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-24T00:52:33"
    },
    {
      "title": "Helen Haines’s condition improves days after losing both legs from alleged attack",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/24/helen-hainess-condition-improves-days-after-losing-both-legs-from-alleged-attack-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Independent MP now serious but stable, according to update from Melbourne’s Alfred hospital</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Independent MP Helen Haines’s condition has been downgraded to serious but stable after she lost both legs following an alleged attack near her electorate office in north-east Victoria on Monday afternoon.</p><p>The Alfred hospital in Melbourne provided an update on Haines’s condition on Saturday morning.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/24/helen-hainess-condition-improves-days-after-losing-both-legs-from-alleged-attack-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-24T00:41:29"
    },
    {
      "title": "Thunderstorms, heavy rain and flash flooding predicted for much of Australia",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/24/thunderstorms-heavy-rain-and-flash-flooding-predicted-for-much-of-australia",
      "description": "<p>Parts of Queensland, Victoria and South Australia can expect severe storms on Saturday, moving into NSW and Tasmania by Sunday</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Severe thunderstorms and heavy rain will sweep across most Australian states this weekend, adding to the deluge in an already drenched Queensland.</p><p>Flash flooding in south-east Queensland this week prompted hundreds of SES callouts and the closure of multiple schools. On Saturday morning, the Bureau of Meteorology had nine flood warnings in place for south Queensland.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/24/thunderstorms-heavy-rain-and-flash-flooding-predicted-for-much-of-australia\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-23T23:26:05"
