    {
      "title": "Jordon Steele-John’s position remains in limbo as Greens prepare for moment in spotlight",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/23/jordan-steele-john-in-limbo-greens-misconduct-allegations-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>David Shoebridge’s newly-minted leadership under pressure over handling of misconduct allegations as Senate estimates looms</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>More than a week after allegations that Greens senator Jordon Steele-John had behaved inappropriately towards women made headlines, his position in the party remains in limbo and its new leader’s handling of the issue in question.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/30/im-up-for-a-red-hot-fight-polarising-new-greens-leader-david-shoebridge-is-taking-on-the-top-1-and-one-nation\">David Shoebridge</a>’s first major challenge at the helm of the federal Greens came earlier this month when the Nine newspapers reported <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/18/greens-senator-jordon-steele-john-says-not-on-leave-blames-david-shoebridge-complaints-ntwnfb\">a three-page letter had been sent to him</a> urging an independent investigation into Steele-John.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/oct/23/jordan-steele-john-in-limbo-greens-misconduct-allegations-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
